  "claim": "The Swiss immigration referendum, February 2014 is an example of relations between Switzerland and the European Union, which was framed by bilateral treaties between Switzerland and the European Union.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Swiss immigration referendum, February 2014. Sentence: The Swiss federal popular initiative \"against mass immigration\" (German: \"Eidgenössische Volksinitiative \"Gegen Masseneinwanderung\"\" , French: \"Initiative populaire « Contre l'immigration de masse »\" , Italian: \"Iniziativa popolare \"Contro l'immigrazione di massa\"\" ) was a referendum that aimed to limit immigration through quotas, as it had been prior to the bilateral treaties between Switzerland and the European Union launched 2002.\nPage: Switzerland–European Union relations. Sentence: The relations between Switzerland and the European Union (EU) are framed by a series of bilateral treaties whereby the Swiss Confederation has adopted various provisions of European Union law in order to participate in the Union's single market.",
